<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Zachary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 752</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Pope Zacharias</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Zachary was a Greek-speaking pope from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a> who held office from 741 to 752. He negotiated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> kings to protect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and supported the church reforms of Boniface in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francia">Francia</a>. When Pippin the Short asked whether the man with real power should be king, Zachary approved, and in 751 Pippin deposed the last Merovingian, Childeric III, beginning the Carolingian alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-zachary.jpg" alt="Pope Zachary" width="320" height="524" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Et%C3%A0_di_papa_Zaccaria,_cappella_del_primicerius_Teodoro,_Madonna_in_trono_con_Theodoto_e_la_moglie,_741-752_(09).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
